      "title": "Reka-style HumanEval prompting",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "The new reka template starts with “human: Complete the following Python function.” It requests concise reasoning in comments without second-guessing, inserts the problem, then opens “ <sep> assistant: ```python\\n” and repeats the problem as the assistant's code prefill.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_cab31787897b4aeda040f9747700697d"]
        },
        {
          "text": "main replaces both {{problem}} placeholders with the HumanEval prompt, encodes the resulting string with special-token handling and BOS enabled, and passes those tokens through the existing Job creation path. The template does not add separate Reka-specific stopping behavior.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_cab31787897b4aeda040f9747700697d", "call_35b473a7af2d4ceba135fc88040fb828"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The tuple's second value is four spaces used when saving prefix + completion.strip(), not an extra suffix appended to the model input. Existing collection still stops at EOS or a non-indented final line and saves task_id/completion records, excluding the conversational wrapper.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_cab31787897b4aeda040f9747700697d", "call_35b473a7af2d4ceba135fc88040fb828"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Repeating the function under the assistant's Python fence appears intended to steer generation toward continuing its body rather than producing a standalone conversational answer. Requesting reasoning as comments is consistent with retaining executable code, but model compliance is not established.",
          "basis": "inference",
          "evidence": ["call_cab31787897b4aeda040f9747700697d", "call_35b473a7af2d4ceba135fc88040fb828"]
        },
        {
          "text": "A standard-library check of the transcribed template and collector expression confirmed two problem copies, the exact assistant boundary, no remaining placeholder, and a four-space-prefixed saved “return x” completion for a synthetic function.",
          "basis": "execution",
